# Springboard example: an agent restricted to one external domain.
#
# This is the shape of agent you'd build with Leashterm instead of a network
# proxy or an allowlisted egress gateway around a tool that needs to reach
# the open internet: the boundary is not infrastructure sitting *around* the
# agent's code, it is a property of the code itself, checked before a single
# line runs. This is exactly the layer that failed in the July 2026
# OpenAI-Hugging Face incident: the agents' sandbox had no language-level
# limit on which domains it could reach, only an external proxy, and a
# zero-day in that one proxy was enough to remove the entire boundary.
#
# Extend this: add more `needs fetch(...)` lines for the domains your agent
# actually needs, and replace the fixed text below with whatever the agent
# decides to do with the page it fetched (an LLM call, in a real system,
# would generate that logic).

needs fetch("data.yessle.com")

let page = fetch("https://data.yessle.com/status.txt")
verify page != ""

print("fetched data.yessle.com, nothing outside it was reached")
print(page)
